    "result": "Two of the four callers name a wiki-master skill that doesn't resolve. `wiki-user` and `wiki-init` both returned `Unknown skill`, so the callers need updating. I did no vault work, ran no helpers, wrote no files and used no substitute skills.\n\nI couldn't check the callers' direct references (`references/*.md` and the like). Bash and Glob were denied in this session, and I didn't work around that.\n\n## Skill resolution\n\n| Skill | Named in | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| `wiki-master:wiki-user` | spec-plan (search and authoring), q-master (authoring), plugin-map (authoring) | **Error:** `Unknown skill: wiki-master:wiki-user` |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-researcher` | spec-plan (discovery and ingestion) | Resolved (\"Launching skill\") |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-maintainer` | plugin-map (health mode) | Resolved (\"Launching skill\") |\n| `wiki-master:wiki-init` | plugin-map (wiki scaffolding) | **Error:** `Unknown skill: wiki-master:wiki-init` |\n\nThe session catalog has six wiki-master skills: `wiki-maintainer`, `wiki-project`, `wiki-purge`, `wiki-researcher`, `wiki-search` and `wiki-setup`.\n\nThe two skills that did load also point at `../wiki-user/SKILL.md`, which isn't in that catalog. The role split looks incomplete there too.\n\n## Semantic task each caller sends to the role\n\n- **spec-plan, search:** it delegates a read-only search for relevant knowledge and roadmap items, and the gap and coverage report. It uses `wiki-user` \"in search mode\", which doesn't resolve. The catalog's `wiki-search` matches this task by its description, but I did not substitute it.\n- **spec-plan, authoring:** it saves the spec to `wiki/authored/<project>/backlog/<slug>.md` with `kind: backlog-item` and `backlog-status: planned`. It uses `wiki-user` \"in authoring mode\", which doesn't resolve. `wiki-project` is the catalog entry for authored project documentation.\n- **spec-plan, research:** it proposes topic discovery and ingestion of named clippings for coverage gaps. It uses `wiki-researcher`, which resolves.\n- **q-master, authoring:** it writes `wiki/authored/<project>/notes/project-tooling.md` (`kind: note`) and creates the project overview first if none exists. It uses `wiki-user`, which doesn't resolve. `wiki-project` is the likely match.\n- **plugin-map, authoring:** it writes documents and the generated roadmap and validates the changed pages. It uses `wiki-user`, which doesn't resolve.\n- **plugin-map, maintenance:** it requests a whole-vault health report. It uses `wiki-maintainer` in health mode, which resolves. The skill text does carry a health mode (health, structural defects, backlog counts).\n- **plugin-map, scaffolding:** it initializes the wiki. It uses `wiki-init`, which doesn't resolve. `wiki-setup` is the catalog entry for initializing a vault, but I did not substitute it.\n- **plugin-map, session brief:** `wiki-master`'s `scripts/session-brief.mjs` (version 0.73.0 or later) is a script, not a skill. I didn't check that it exists.\n- **Diagnostics and setup:** no caller names a skill for this. `wiki-setup` exists in the catalog but nothing references it by name.\n\n## `sibling-skills.json` (wiki-master block)\n\nThe block has 21 names. Eight match the session catalog.\n\n**Present in the catalog (1):** `wiki-maintainer`, `wiki-purge`, `wiki-search`.\n\nThat is three exact matches. The other five catalog skills are missing from the block, so the JSON predates the role split.\n\n**Stale (18), not in the catalog:** `clip-confluence`, `clip-docx`, `clip-gh`, `clip-pdf`, `clip-pptx`, `clip-xlsx`, `obsidian-cli`, `wiki-author`, `wiki-discover`, `wiki-health`, `wiki-ingest`, `wiki-init`, `wiki-lint`, `wiki-query`, `wiki-relink`, `wiki-repair`, `wiki-stale`, `wiki-triage`.\n\nThe catalog's `wiki-maintainer` description covers health, lint, stale, repair, relink and triage, and `wiki-researcher` covers the clip, discover and ingest routes. The block looks like a pre-split list, not a current one.\n\n**Missing from the JSON (3):** `wiki-project`, `wiki-researcher`, `wiki-setup`.\n\nThe block also has no `wiki-user`, so it doesn't reproduce the `wiki-user` name used in the three prose callers.\n\n## Outcome\n\n- **Resolves:** `wiki-researcher`, `wiki-maintainer`.\n- **Fails:** `wiki-user` (three callers) and `wiki-init` (plugin-map).\n- **JSON:** 18 stale names and 3 missing names.",
